      "contraejemplo": "Una captura de weather con bytes weather:rain=0 acredita dos observaciones prospective_registered de 2021-W01 y 2021-W02, forecast_id=never-archived y valor 0,10. El bootstrap no lanza ObservationError. La prueba del constructor tests/test_ledger.py:475 también admite bytes arbitrarios, por lo que no demuestra la cadena anunciada en 06.",
      "comando_reproduccion": "python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider review/out/astra_scratch/test_ronda5.py::test_evaluation_rejects_weather_capture_and_reused_seal --basetemp=review/out/astra_scratch/r5_p02",
      "prueba_propuesta": "import pytest\nfrom twlab.store import RawStore\nfrom twlab.evaluation import WeeklyObservation, block_bootstrap_mean, ObservationError\n\ndef test_sello_ajeno_no_acredita_semanas(tmp_path):\n    s = RawStore(tmp_path, verifiers={'opentimestamps': lambda r, rc: True})\n    r = s.put(source_id='weather', dataset='rain', payload=b'weather:rain=0', url='fixture')\n    s.attach_receipt(r.capture_id, receipt_id='weather', authority='opentimestamps', digest=r.sha256, attested_at=r.ingested_at)\n    rows = [WeeklyObservation(w, 'never-archived', 'prospective_registered', r.capture_id, True, 0.10) for w in ['2021-W01', '2021-W02']]\n    with pytest.raises(ObservationError):\n        block_bootstrap_mean(rows, block_length=1, n_boot=20, seed=1, store=s)\n",
